g.\nUse all clearly applicable taxonomy parents. Fruit and vegetable here mean harvested food, not a whole living plant. A fruit is food but is not tagged plant. eating means an edible item, never a cup or an animal's act of eating; use grazing or hunting for animal behavior.\nA module description must explain only that axis. Classification describes kind, shape describes visible geometry/parts, function describes use/behavior. Do not leak shape or purpose into classification descriptions merely to distinguish labels.\nUse canonical tag meanings consistently. A hollow drinking vessel has hollow and opening whether cup or mug. Standard drink containers use holding_liquid and serving_drink. Do not arbitrarily vary synonyms across categories.\nFor a polysemous category preserve ambiguity on the affected axes rather than merging incompatible meanings as known. For diamond do not combine geometric_shape and natural_object. For nail use the catalog Korean name to distinguish metal fastener from fingernail, retaining a note if uncertain.\nTypical sketch conventions, not rare variants: baseball has curved stitched seams, basketball has panel division lines; blackberry is an aggregate bumpy fruit, blueberry is a single smooth berry. Describe typical features, not an assertion that any source drawing was inspected.\nChurch is a worship building, house is a dwelling; clarinet usually a straight woodwind tube, saxophone usually curved with a flared bell; key opens a lock, nail fastens by being driven in. Use the supplied reusable tags when these distinctions apply.\nNatural water bodies have recognizable geometry even when they have no human purpose. Ocean is broad open water with waves; pond is bounded inland water. Do not manufacture a function just to avoid not_applicable.\nuncertain is reserved for material ambiguity or a genuinely missing vocabulary term. A variation between individuals alone does not invalidate a representative feature. When a useful tag is missing, expla